name  = churn
shape = a long-lived table under insert/delete churn with a BOUNDED live set
args  = 200000 2000
claim = the shape Mere is structurally bad at, kept in the suite for that
        reason. A region is a bump arena: `map_delete` returns nothing and an
        overwrite leaves the old deep copy behind, so a naive Mere table grows
        with the TOTAL number of operations while every garbage-collected
        runtime here tracks the LIVE SET instead. bench_regionloop.mere is the
        language's answer (`region R loop`, v0.1.296) and is in the table next
        to the naive version, so the row shows both the cost and the tool. A
        suite that only carried workloads its subject wins is not a
        measurement.

# The sweep is the point of this benchmark. Operation count is held constant
# and the LIVE SET is doubled: an implementation whose delete is O(1) draws a
# flat line, and one whose delete shifts the table draws a doubling one.
sweep_axis = live-set size, at a fixed 100k operations
sweep = 100000 250 | 100000 500 | 100000 1000 | 100000 2000 | 100000 4000

# Measured 43,298,448 B at v0.1.316 for the NAIVE program at `args` -- 200k
# operations over a 2,000-entry live set, so ~43 MB is retained to hold what is
# at any moment ~100 KB of data. That ratio is the finding, and the ceiling is
# here so a change to it is announced rather than discovered.
#
# The band covers BOTH Mere rows, and the bound is on every arena rather than
# on the default one -- since v0.1.319 the meter reports named arenas too, so
# a program that moves its allocation into `region R loop` no longer drops out
# of its own gate. The two rows sit at opposite ends on purpose:
#
#   naive       43.4 MB, all of it in the default region, none of it returned
#   region loop 62.4 MB cumulative across 42 arenas, 3.1 MB resident at peak
#
# The loop allocates MORE in total (it copies the live set into a fresh arena
# once per generation) and holds 20x less at once. That trade is the whole
# claim of the construct, and until the meter could see named arenas only the
# second half of it was measurable -- through peak RSS, the figure that does
# not reproduce.
alloc_min = 25165824
alloc_max = 83886080

# The number the region loop exists to control. Deterministic, unlike the RSS
# that used to be the only evidence for it.
peak_max = 8388608
